  "package_id": "berge-c5-saturation",
  "formal_scope": "Lean 4.35.0 proves, for actual three-uniform hypergraphs on Fin n, Berge-C₅s with distinct vertices and distinct hyperedges, and saturation under every absent triple, that every m with ⌈2(n − 1)/3⌉ ≤ m ≤ n − 2 is the size of a saturated hypergraph for n ≥ 14, that sat₃(n, Berge-C₅) ≤ ⌈2(n − 1)/3⌉ for n ≥ 7, that n − 1 is a saturated size when 4 divides n − 1, and the exact values for n ≤ 7, through a general rooted-gluing theorem and nine kernel-checked pieces without native_decide. The endpoints ⌈(2n − 8)/3⌉ and ⌈(2n − 8)/3⌉ + 1 for n ≥ 47, the cone classification and the expansion theorems have conventional proofs and exhaustive construction checks, and the values for 8 ≤ n ≤ 11 rest on exhaustive certificates checked by an independent C++ verifier.",
